[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#e6a23c]Your farms, ready when you return[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
ChunkLoader gives players a simple way to keep a Minecraft chunk running without staying nearby. Place a loader, manage its remaining time through an inventory menu, and refuel it with experience levels, money, or another loader item.

Use temporary loaders for a survival economy or infinite loaders for permanent infrastructure. Each loader keeps one complete 16 x 16 chunk active, including the full vertical build area. Machines continue working, crops receive Paper's native random ticks, and inactive standard spawners can operate through ChunkLoader's farm simulation.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#e6a23c]Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Timed or infinite loaders[/B] - Issue durations such as 30m, 2h, 1d, or infinite.
[*][B]Three ways to refuel[/B] - Spend XP levels, use an optional Vault economy, or merge another loader's time.
[*][B]Simple management menus[/B] - Right-click to manage a loader; left-click to confirm removal.
[*][B]Offline farm operation[/B] - Keep furnaces, hoppers, redstone, crops, and supported mob spawners working without nearby players.
[*][B]Native floating text[/B] - Display the remaining time above each loader with no hologram plugin required.
[*][B]Ownership and limits[/B] - Control who can manage loaders, limit placements per player, and restrict worlds.
[*][B]Block protection[/B] - Protect registered loaders against explosions, pistons, fire, fluid replacement, and entity changes.
[*][B]Chunk visualization[/B] - Show personal particles around nearby loader chunks without loading extra terrain.
[*][B]Reliable overlap handling[/B] - Several loaders can share a chunk without removing each other's chunk ticket.
[*][B]Persistent data[/B] - Retain ownership and remaining time across restarts with validated JSON and atomic backups.
[*][B]Server-friendly work budgets[/B] - Bound supplemental farm work and distribute it between active chunks.
[*][B]Open source[/B] - MIT licensed, with a public API for other plugins to grant shared loader access.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#e6a23c]Get started in a minute[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Install the JAR on a supported Paper server and restart.
[*]Run [ICODE]/chunkloader give YourName 2h[/ICODE] as an operator or from the console.
[*]Place the supplied loader block in the chunk you want to keep active.
[*]Right-click it to add time, or use [ICODE]/chunkloader show[/ICODE] to view nearby loader chunks.
[/LIST]

By default, one purchase adds [B]30 minutes[/B] for [B]10 XP levels[/B] or [B]5000 currency units[/B]. Prices, duration, material, limits, messages, and display options are configurable. Money purchases require Vault and an economy provider; XP and item refueling work without them.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#e6a23c]Commands at a glance[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[CODE]/chunkloader help
/chunkloader show
/chunkloader list [page]
/chunkloader give <player|all|@a> <duration> [amount]
/chunkloader reload
/chunkloader settings[/CODE]
Aliases: [B]/cl[/B] and [B]/cloader[/B]. Permissions use the [B]chunkloader.[/B] prefix. Players can manage their own loaders; administrators can manage all loaders.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#e6a23c]Requirements and compatibility[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Server:[/B] Paper 1.21.11 through 26.3. Paper is required; Spigot-only servers and Folia are not supported.
[*][B]Java:[/B] Java 21 for Minecraft 1.21.11; Java 25 for Minecraft 26.x.
[*][B]Optional:[/B] Vault plus a supported economy provider for money refueling.
[*][B]Verified builds:[/B] Paper 1.21.11/132, 26.1.2/74, 26.2/134, and 26.3/218.
[/LIST]

For operation while nobody is connected, set [ICODE]pause-when-empty-seconds=-1[/ICODE] in [ICODE]server.properties[/ICODE]. Timers pause when the server or the loader's world is offline. Each loader covers one chunk; it does not create a configurable loading radius.

Custom spawner rules and plugins that depend on exact native event ordering may behave differently with the public-API spawner simulation. Natural mob spawning, trial spawners, and farms that require player interaction retain Minecraft's own requirements. Existing data and items from other loader plugins are not imported automatically.

